# The network of "Build the shop's gateway", the NAT labs' network with two
# public addresses on gw's wan: the shop's private network behind its
# gateway, and a small internet.
#
#   office 10.1.0.10 --+                                               +-- srv 203.0.113.10
#                      [shop]-- gw --[isp]-- inet --[internet]---------+
#   app 10.1.0.20 -----+   10.1.0.1  198.51.100.2,.3  .1  203.0.113.1   +-- client 203.0.113.20
#
# gw is a host to netlab: forwarding is off until its own /etc/sysctl.d says
# otherwise, and its firewall is whatever its /etc/nftables.conf holds once
# the learner enables nftables@gw. inet has no route to 10.0.0.0/8: private
# addresses aren't routed on the internet. srv is the payment provider (443,
# holdserver-srv, behind its own firewall, which accepts 443 only from
# 198.51.100.3) and a web server (80). The app's web app is nginx on 8443;
# its database and SSH stand-ins (5432, 22) are shop-backend.service.
machine office
machine app
machine gw
machine inet router
machine srv
machine client

lan shop office:eth0=10.1.0.10/24 app:eth0=10.1.0.20/24 gw:lan=10.1.0.1/24
lan isp gw:wan=198.51.100.2/24,198.51.100.3/24 inet:isp=198.51.100.1/24
lan internet inet:pub=203.0.113.1/24 srv:eth0=203.0.113.10/24 client:eth0=203.0.113.20/24

route office default via 10.1.0.1
route app default via 10.1.0.1
route gw default via 198.51.100.1
route srv default via 203.0.113.1
route client default via 203.0.113.1

run app nginx
run srv nftables nginx
